76589e9a-5ae5-43aa-b0ce-a2f4e3248268 submission: {"title":"Crown Opening — Supplied Sealed-Envelope Account","text":"Members of the jury, the Crown will present Mira’s supplied account: “I saw Fictional Morgan hand the sealed envelope to Fictional Ellis. I do not know what the envelope contained.” (E-001.) This permitted material attributes Mira’s observation; it does not establish the contents or guilt. The Crown bears the burden of proving the supplied condition, receipt of the sealed envelope from Fictional Morgan, beyond a reasonable doubt. You must assess the account’s credibility and sufficiency independently."}
76a41a7f-87fe-422a-bb6d-627b8cfc1f51 submission: {"title":"Defence Opening — Limited Use of Mira’s Account","text":"Members of the jury, the Crown’s opening identifies Mira’s account: “I saw Fictional Morgan hand the sealed envelope to Fictional Ellis. I do not know what the envelope contained.” (E-001.) The Defence agrees that E-001 may attribute Mira’s account, but its permitted use does not establish the envelope’s contents or guilt. The supplied fictional condition remains receipt of the sealed envelope from Fictional Morgan, and the Crown bears the burden of proving it beyond a reasonable doubt."}
